body:
This assertion is now happy-dom specific: in jsdom, reading `style.backgroundColor` after setting a hex value is typically normalized to an `rgb(...)` string. Since `@object-ui/plugin-report`'s local Vitest config uses `environment: 'jsdom'` (packages/plugin-report/vite.config.ts), running `pnpm --filter @object-ui/plugin-report test` may fail. Consider normalizing the color before asserting (or accepting both hex and rgb formats), or aligning the plugin-report test environment with the repo’s root happy-dom config.
```suggestion
    const wonBackground = wonCell?.style.backgroundColor;
    expect(wonBackground === '#bbf7d0' || wonBackground === 'rgb(187, 247, 208)').toBe(true);
```
